1
00:04:08,181 --> 00:04:14,181
Welcome to the Kaufman surreal-neorealism tale in a dull world of sameness.

2
00:08:16,363 --> 00:08:22,363
Anomalisa is a animation, drama, romance film directed by Charlie Kaufman.

3
00:12:24,545 --> 00:12:30,545
An inspirational speaker becomes reinvigorated after meeting a
lively woman who shakes up his mundane existence.

4
00:16:32,727 --> 00:16:38,727
Michael Stone (voice), played by David Thewlis.

5
00:20:40,909 --> 00:20:46,909
Lisa Hesselman (voice), played by Jennifer Jason Leigh.

6
00:24:49,090 --> 00:24:55,090
Everyone Else (voice), played by Tom Noonan.

7
00:28:57,272 --> 00:29:03,272
Anomalisa is a 2015 American adult animated film directed by Charlie Kaufman and Duke Johnson from a screenplay by Kaufman, based on
his 2005 audio play of the same name that explores the Fregoli delusion, a term Kaufman used as a pen name for himself.

8
00:33:05,454 --> 00:33:11,454
It incorporates elements of psychological drama, romantic comedy, and self-reflexive fiction,
in a similar vein as Kaufman's film Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mind.

9
00:37:13,636 --> 00:37:19,636
Anomalisa follows the British middle-aged customer service expert Michael Stone (David Thewlis), who perceives everyone (Tom
Noonan) as identical except for Lisa Hesselman (Jennifer Jason Leigh), whom he meets in a Cincinnati hotel.

10
00:41:21,818 --> 00:41:27,818
Kaufman's audio play premiered in Los Angeles, and featured
the voices of Thewlis, Noonan, and Leigh.

11
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
He opposed adapting the play into a film, fearing loss of artistic merit, but began
exploring the idea in 2012 after incorporating edits to the script.

12
00:49:38,181 --> 00:49:44,181
Filming faced delays as Starburns Industries initially secured production funding on Kickstarter only
to adapt the play as a short film, with stop-motion animation beginning in late 2013.

13
00:53:46,363 --> 00:53:52,363
The filmmakers faced struggles with animation
technology, a notoriously laborious medium.

14
00:57:54,545 --> 00:58:00,545
This was alleviated after Paramount Pictures joined production,
enabling the film to be expanded to a feature.

15
01:02:02,727 --> 01:02:08,727
Anomalisa premiered at the Telluride Film Festival on September 4,
2015, and was theatrically released in the U.S.

16
01:06:10,909 --> 01:06:16,909
on December 30 by Paramount Pictures.

17
01:10:19,090 --> 01:10:25,090
The film received critical acclaim, with praise for its
screenplay, direction, and thematic content.

18
01:14:27,272 --> 01:14:33,272
It was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Animated Feature, the first R-rated animated film to be nominated
in this category, and was nominated for the Golden Globe Award for Best Animated Feature Film.

19
01:18:35,454 --> 01:18:41,454
It won the Grand Jury Prize at the 72nd Venice International
Film Festival, the first animated film to do so.

20
01:22:43,636 --> 01:22:49,636
The film explores themes of depression, nightmare,
love at first sight, melancholy, puppet.

21
01:26:51,818 --> 01:26:57,818
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and thought_provoking.
